<title>FRANCE: TABLE-Danone H1 sales up 5.3 percent.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Danone H1 sales up 5.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>Turnover					43,808    vs   41,591</p>
<p>Western Europe</p>
<p>	- dairy products			  11,353    vs   11,141</p>
<p>	- grocery products			 7,658    vs    7,902</p>
<p>	- biscuits				   5,963    vs    5,866</p>
<p>	- beverages				  7,569    vs    7,678</p>
<p>	- containers				 3,279    vs    3,335</p>
<p>	International				9,418    vs    6,945</p>
<p>NOTE - Food group Danone gave its sales figures in a statement. It said sales rose 5.3 percent.</p>
<p>It said that after an unsettled first quarter group sales rebounded sharply in the second quarter despite unseasonably cold weather in June.</p>
<p>Currency conversion differences, due mainly to rises in the U.S. dollar, the Italian lira and the sterling added 1.1 billion francs.</p>
<p>Changes in the scope the scope of consolidation, reflecting the consolidation of new acquisitions outside western Europe added 750 million francs.</p>
<p>First half earnings will be announced on September 9.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
